; A customer domain with nothing wrong with it.
;
; The end-to-end fixture for the check pipeline: SPF authorising the platform,
; a DKIM selector the platform issued, an enforcing DMARC policy, a null MX
; because this domain only sends, and two nameservers holding the same serial.
;
; Every other fixture here isolates one fault. This one exists so that a clean
; run across six checks is reachable and tested — a checker that finds something
; to fix on every domain is a checker nobody reads. Clean is not silent: the
; null MX is still reported, at info severity, because a dashboard should say
; that this domain accepts no mail.
;
; Served by dns-auth and dns-divergent both. Keep the two in step, serial
; included, or this stops testing a healthy domain and starts testing drift.
$ORIGIN customer.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN NS   ns-divergent.test.

; The platform's include, and nothing else authorised.
@                   IN TXT  "v=spf1 include:one.spf.test -all"

; RFC 7505: this domain sends and does not receive, and says so.
@                   IN MX   0 .

; Enforcing, with reports going to the domain itself so no external
; authorisation is needed.
_dmarc              IN TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc@customer.test"

; The selector the platform issued.
pg1._domainkey         IN TXT ( "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEApbBuIv1NwQ/rmgGPN8OufvLBfd2asvyk4ajVkiW2CsC12MohickhGufJPsGNyO/ZXD4b/HnClukz07BZwpJe80wz0w/AfhJCqM8F3v/aVHF7wWnd9wBBPBroTL7kNx5u39NnBZZj8SYJF7zNaQ3rud4ekF+GAyTovT7MUfXHQBgEZn0n5Y4dN7b7VEMi4/97T"
                                "DCNDJucFywdDmbJ9r6LaCu+l+gWfZGl4rDimTJCw3oCQIpCOGlNrWPwxRLuB0sLR2gR1GT9EqBg3yGforXasq2wqBuZlpI1YXmdldEZh3VRIyft4TeVTHRJAf7/TKuAINb8+LOoXHj5hFYl+C4zUQIDAQAB" )

; RFC 6376 3.6.1: an empty p= is revocation, not corruption. Reporting it
; as malformed would tell someone to fix a record they revoked on purpose.
